# Binary file types
#
# These are stored as ordinary Git files and marked binary, so Git never
# rewrites their line endings or tries to diff or merge them as text.
#
# Git LFS is deliberately not used. This repository has never held LFS content
# apart from four font pointers whose objects were never uploaded (commit
# d004268), which made every clone and the upstream sync fail with
# "404 Object does not exist on the server". A commit made from an environment
# that cannot upload LFS objects would repeat that failure, and every consumer
# (CI, Vercel, the deployment sync) would need LFS support. The repository
# integrity test (tests/repository-integrity.test.mjs) fails if an LFS rule or
# pointer file comes back.

